{
 "esm": "1.2.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "LevelSetTendencyWRFFire",
  "description": "The level-set propagation equation of fire_behavior (physics/level_set_mod.F90 Calc_tend_ls; Munoz-Esparza et al. 2018) as a PDE on a uniform 2-D grid: d psi/dt = -R |grad psi| + nu |R| (dx d2psi/dx2 + dy d2psi/dy2), the Hamilton-Jacobi front propagation with the rate of spread R normal to the front plus a grid-scaled artificial viscosity, together with the per-axis upwind derivatives diff2x, diff2y and the front normal (nvx, nvy) = (diff2x, diff2y)/sqrt(|grad psi|^2 + eps) that ROSWRFFire consumes. |grad psi| is written as the compound sqrt(D(psi,x)^2 + D(psi,y)^2) and the per-axis derivatives as D(psi,x), D(psi,y); the DISCRETISATION IS SELECTED BY THE RULES EACH TEST IMPORTS from EarthSciDiscretizations grids/cartesian_uniform_2d: fire_upwinding = 4 (classical Godunov) = godunov_norm_D2_dirichlet_bc for the norm and godunov_upwind_D1x/D1y_extrapolate_bc (max(D-,0) - min(D+,0)) for the normal; fire_upwinding = 9 (the DEFAULT, hybrid WENO5/ENO1) = weno5_eno1_norm_D2_extrapolate_bc and weno5_eno1_D1x/D1y_extrapolate_bc, whose free names wind_u, wind_v (the mid-flame wind that selects the WENO upwind side), bdy_eno1_cells (BDY_ENO1 = 10) and weno_band_cells (fire_lsm_band_ngp = 4) are this model's inputs and parameters, and whose wall closure is fire_behavior's own guarded linear-extrapolation halo (Extrapol_var_at_bdys). The second derivatives of the viscosity term use the centred rules with the matching wall closure (central_D2x/D2y_dirichlet_bc for the Godunov test, central_D2x/D2y_extrapolate_bc for the default scheme). R is supplied as an input field (it depends on the normal, tested in ROSWRFFire); the propagation term, the viscosity, the per-axis derivatives and the normal are what this component asserts. Tests: the ls_tend dumps of Runge-Kutta stage 1 of step 20 (t = 10 s) of test7 with fire_upwinding = 4 (39 original + 52 normal assertions, interior cells only because the Dirichlet-closed Godunov norm rule treats the walls differently) and with the default fire_upwinding = 9 (112 assertions including wall-strip and wall cells), real32, rel 1e-5 to 2e-5. Coupling hook (added 2026-09-21): the rate-of-spread field the PDE uses is `ros`, which equals the consumer-supplied `ros_supplied` everywhere except the single cell (i_coupled, j_coupled), where it is the coupling-target parameter ros_in; i_coupled = 0 by default, so nothing changes unless a coupling document sets it. couplings/wildlandfire_behavior.esm uses it to drive one cell's spread rate from the mounted Anderson13FuelTable -> FuelMoistureWRFFire -> RothermelWRFFire -> ROSWRFFire chain. fire_upwinding = 7 (pure WENO5) added 2026-09-21 as a third regime: it is case (9) with the band test removed, so it needs no new rule -- only weno_band_cells past the domain diagonal. fire_upwinding = 10 (WENO5/ENO1 with a cosine blending zone) added 2026-09-21 as a fourth regime, lowered by a new ESD rule; it is the first smooth partition-of-unity operator in that library. fire_upwinding = 8 (hybrid WENO3/ENO1) added 2026-09-21 as a fifth regime, lowered by a new ESD rule family weno3_eno1_norm_D2_extrapolate_bc + weno3_eno1_D1x/D1y_extrapolate_bc: case (8) is case (9) with Select_weno5 replaced by Select_weno3, but there was no WENO3 on cartesian_uniform_2d at all and the library's only WENO3 elsewhere is a 1-D WENO-Z reconstruction with different nonlinear weights, so the classical Jiang-Shu pair had to be transcribed fresh.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "wildland_fire",
   "fire_behavior",
   "wrf-fire",
   "level-set",
   "pde"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "NCAR Community Fire Behavior Model (fire_behavior), develop @ eb77580; instrumented fork ctessum-claude/fire_behavior branch earthsciml-instrumented (c9dda02)."
   },
   {
    "citation": "Munoz-Esparza, D., Kosovic, B., Jimenez, P.A., Coen, J.L. (2018). An accurate fire-spread algorithm in the Weather Research and Forecasting model using the level-set method. J. Adv. Model. Earth Syst. 10, 908-926.",
    "doi": "10.1002/2017MS001108"
   },
   {
    "citation": "Osher, S., Sethian, J.A. (1988). Fronts propagating with curvature-dependent speed. J. Comput. Phys. 79, 12-49.",
    "doi": "10.1016/0021-9991(88)90002-2"
   }
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NX": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 80,
   "description": "Fire-grid cells along x (test7: 80)."
  },
  "NY": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 80,
   "description": "Fire-grid cells along y."
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "LevelSetTendencyWRFFire": {
   "expression_template_imports": [{"ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/grid.esm", "bindings": {"NX": "NX", "NY": "NY"}}],
   "variables": {
    "psi": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "x",
      "y"
     ],
     "description": "Level-set function over the [x, y] fire grid (fire_behavior lfn; negative inside the burnt area, a signed distance after reinitialisation)."
    },
    "ros": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "shape": [
      "x",
      "y"
     ],
     "description": "Effective rate-of-spread field entering the PDE: ros_supplied everywhere except the single cell (i_coupled, j_coupled), where it is the coupling target ros_in. With the default i_coupled = 0 no cell matches and ros is ros_supplied, so a standalone run is unchanged; a coupling document that mounts ROSWRFFire beside this component sets i_coupled/j_coupled and drives ros_in, which makes d psi/dt at that cell depend on the whole fuel -> moisture -> Rothermel -> ROS chain. Same idiom as s_coupled in fire_flux_to_atmosphere_wrffire.esm."
    },
    "wind_u": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "shape": [
      "x",
      "y"
     ],
     "description": "Mid-flame wind x-component uf on the fire grid (input field; free name wind_u of the hybrid WENO5/ENO1 rules, whose WENO upwind side is selected by the sign of (grad4 psi . U) d4 psi). Not read by the Godunov rules."
    },
    "wind_v": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "shape": [
      "x",
      "y"
     ],
     "description": "Mid-flame wind y-component vf on the fire grid (input field; free name wind_v of the hybrid rules)."
    },
    "x0": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Left domain edge (grid free name)."
    },
    "y0": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Bottom domain edge (grid free name)."
    },
    "Lx": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 2000.0,
     "description": "Domain width NX dx (test7: 80 x 25 m)."
    },
    "Ly": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 2000.0,
     "description": "Domain height NY dy."
    },
    "dx": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "x spacing Lx/NX (grid free name)."
    },
    "dy": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "y spacing Ly/NY (grid free name)."
    },
    "fire_viscosity": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.4,
     "description": "Artificial viscosity coefficient nu (namelist fire_viscosity = fire_viscosity_bg = 0.4 in test7, so the near-front band has the same value and the coefficient is uniform)."
    },
    "grad_mag": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "x",
      "y"
     ],
     "description": "|grad psi| of the selected scheme (fire_behavior grad / grad_norm_ls): with the Godunov rule (fire_upwinding = 4) sqrt(max(D-x,0)^2 + min(D+x,0)^2 + max(D-y,0)^2 + min(D+y,0)^2); with the hybrid rule (fire_upwinding = 9, the default) sqrt(diff2x^2 + diff2y^2) of the WENO5/ENO1 per-axis derivatives. Written as the compound sqrt(D(psi,x)^2 + D(psi,y)^2); the norm rule imported by the test selects the scheme."
    },
    "psi_xx": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1/m",
     "shape": [
      "x",
      "y"
     ],
     "description": "d2 psi/dx2 by the centred second-difference rule; fire_behavior's (diffrx - difflx) = dx psi_xx."
    },
    "psi_yy": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1/m",
     "shape": [
      "x",
      "y"
     ],
     "description": "d2 psi/dy2 by the centred second-difference rule."
    },
    "tend_adv": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "shape": [
      "x",
      "y"
     ],
     "description": "Hamilton-Jacobi propagation term -ros |grad psi|."
    },
    "tend_visc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "shape": [
      "x",
      "y"
     ],
     "description": "Artificial viscosity nu |ros| (dx psi_xx + dy psi_yy): fire_behavior adds fire_viscosity |ros| ((diffrx - difflx) + (diffry - diffly)), a grid-scaled Laplacian that vanishes with the mesh."
    },
    "tend": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "shape": [
      "x",
      "y"
     ],
     "description": "Level-set tendency d psi/dt = tend_adv + tend_visc (Calc_tend_ls tend)."
    },
    "bdy_eno1_cells": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 10,
     "description": "Width in cells of the wall band where fire_behavior always uses first-order ENO1 (BDY_ENO1 = 10, a compile-time constant of level_set_mod.F90); free name of the hybrid rules."
    },
    "weno_band_cells": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 4,
     "description": "Half-width in cells of the band |psi| < weno_band_cells dx around the front where the hybrid scheme uses WENO5 (namelist fire_lsm_band_ngp = 4); free name of the hybrid rules."
    },
    "gL": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Prescribed level-set value on the left x wall read by the Dirichlet-closed rules (free name of the imported EarthSciDiscretizations rules). Read only by the Dirichlet-closed Godunov norm rule of the fire_upwinding = 4 test; the hybrid rules of the default scheme use fire_behavior's own guarded linear-extrapolation halo instead and do not read it."
    },
    "gR": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Prescribed level-set value on the right x wall read by the Dirichlet-closed rules (free name of the imported EarthSciDiscretizations rules). Read only by the Dirichlet-closed Godunov norm rule of the fire_upwinding = 4 test; the hybrid rules of the default scheme use fire_behavior's own guarded linear-extrapolation halo instead and do not read it."
    },
    "gB": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Prescribed level-set value on the bottom y wall read by the Dirichlet-closed rules (free name of the imported EarthSciDiscretizations rules). Read only by the Dirichlet-closed Godunov norm rule of the fire_upwinding = 4 test; the hybrid rules of the default scheme use fire_behavior's own guarded linear-extrapolation halo instead and do not read it."
    },
    "gT": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Prescribed level-set value on the top y wall read by the Dirichlet-closed rules (free name of the imported EarthSciDiscretizations rules). Read only by the Dirichlet-closed Godunov norm rule of the fire_upwinding = 4 test; the hybrid rules of the default scheme use fire_behavior's own guarded linear-extrapolation halo instead and do not read it."
    },
    "nv_eps": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 1.1920928955078125e-07,
     "description": "Regularisation of the normal's denominator sqrt(|grad psi|^2 + eps): fire_behavior's EPS = epsilon(0.0) of its default real32 kind."
    },
    "psi_x": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": ["x", "y"],
     "description": "Per-axis upwind derivative diff2x of the selected scheme: for fire_upwinding = 4 the Godunov-upwind quantity max(D-x psi, 0) - min(D+x psi, 0) (godunov_upwind_D1x_extrapolate_bc; a magnitude for negative slopes, N44), for fire_upwinding = 9 the hybrid WENO5/ENO1 derivative (weno5_eno1_D1x_extrapolate_bc). Written as D(psi, x); the rule imported by the test selects the scheme."
    },
    "psi_y": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": ["x", "y"],
     "description": "Per-axis upwind derivative diff2y of the selected scheme (see psi_x); D(psi, y)."
    },
    "nvx": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": ["x", "y"],
     "description": "x-component of the front normal, psi_x / sqrt(|grad psi|^2 + eps) (Calc_tend_ls nvx); the input ROSWRFFire takes for the wind and slope projections."
    },
    "nvy": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1", "shape": ["x", "y"], "description": "y-component of the front normal, psi_y / sqrt(|grad psi|^2 + eps) (nvy)."},
    "ros_supplied": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "shape": ["x", "y"],
     "description": "Rate of spread normal to the front at each cell as supplied by the consumer (ROSWRFFire ros, itself a function of the upwind normal); the operator assembly is tested independently of the normal computation."
    },
    "i_coupled": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "x index (1-based) of the cell whose rate of spread is taken from ros_in; 0 disables the replacement."
    },
    "j_coupled": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "y index (1-based) of the cell whose rate of spread is taken from ros_in; 0 disables the replacement."
    },
    "ros_in": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Coupling target: rate of spread of cell (i_coupled, j_coupled), supplied by a mounted ROSWRFFire through a variable_map param_to_var edge."
    },
    "pi_blend": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "fire_behavior's pi, taken from the fire constants library. It is a free name the fire_upwinding = 10 blending rule reads; the hard-edged fire_upwinding = 9 and Godunov rules never reference it, so it is inert in those regimes."
    }
   },
   "equations": [
    {
     "lhs": "dx",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       "Lx",
       "NX"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "dy",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       "Ly",
       "NY"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": {
      "op": "ic",
      "args": [
       "psi"
      ]
     },
     "rhs": {
      "op": "input_psi",
      "args": []
     }
    },
    {"lhs": "ros_supplied", "rhs": {"op": "input_ros", "args": []}},
    {
     "lhs": "ros",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "output_idx": ["i", "j"],
      "args": [],
      "ranges": {"i": {"from": "x"}, "j": {"from": "y"}},
      "expr": {"op": "ifelse", "args": [{"op": "==", "args": ["i", "i_coupled"]}, {"op": "ifelse", "args": [{"op": "==", "args": ["j", "j_coupled"]}, "ros_in", {"op": "index", "args": ["ros_supplied", "i", "j"]}]}, {"op": "index", "args": ["ros_supplied", "i", "j"]}]}
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "wind_u",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "input_wind_u",
      "args": []
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "wind_v",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "input_wind_v",
      "args": []
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "grad_mag",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "sqrt",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "^",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
             "psi"
            ],
            "wrt": "x"
           },
           2
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "^",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
             "psi"
            ],
            "wrt": "y"
           },
           2
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {"lhs": "psi_x", "rhs": {"op": "D", "args": ["psi"], "wrt": "x"}},
    {"lhs": "psi_y", "rhs": {"op": "D", "args": ["psi"], "wrt": "y"}},
    {
     "lhs": "nvx",
     "rhs": {"op": "/", "args": ["psi_x", {"op": "sqrt", "args": [{"op": "+", "args": [{"op": "^", "args": ["grad_mag", 2]}, "nv_eps"]}]}]}
    },
    {
     "lhs": "nvy",
     "rhs": {"op": "/", "args": ["psi_y", {"op": "sqrt", "args": [{"op": "+", "args": [{"op": "^", "args": ["grad_mag", 2]}, "nv_eps"]}]}]}
    },
    {
     "lhs": "psi_xx",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "D",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "D",
        "args": [
         "psi"
        ],
        "wrt": "x"
       }
      ],
      "wrt": "x"
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "psi_yy",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "D",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "D",
        "args": [
         "psi"
        ],
        "wrt": "y"
       }
      ],
      "wrt": "y"
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "tend_adv",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         "ros"
        ]
       },
       "grad_mag"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "tend_visc",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "fire_viscosity",
       {
        "op": "abs",
        "args": [
         "ros"
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           "dx",
           "psi_xx"
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           "dy",
           "psi_yy"
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "tend",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
       "tend_adv",
       "tend_visc"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": {
      "op": "D",
      "args": [
       "psi"
      ],
      "wrt": "t"
     },
     "rhs": "tend"
    },
    {"lhs": "pi_blend", "rhs": "par.pi"}
   ],
   "tests": [
     {
       "id": "weno5_step20_stage1",
       "description": "Reference: NCAR fire_behavior test7 (80x80 fire cells of 25 m, dt = 0.5 s, num_tiles = 1) with its default level-set scheme (fire_upwinding = 9), default real32 build, dumped in-model by the ctessum-claude/fire_behavior fork (branch earthsciml-instrumented, commit c9dda02, based on NCAR fire_behavior eb77580, three commits before v1.0.0; -DESM_DUMP=ON): ls_tend dump call 58 = Runge-Kutta stage 1 of step 20 (t = 10 s). The inputs psi, ros, wind_u and wind_v are the full 80x80 dumped lfn, ros, uf and vf fields injected as [x, y] const fields. grad_mag, tend_adv and tend are checked at all four corners, cells on each wall, cells inside the 10-cell ENO1 wall band, cells within the WENO band of the front (|psi| < 100 m) and far-field ENO1 cells. The rules reproduce the dump over the whole field to the tolerances used here (checked offline). fire_viscosity = fire_viscosity_bg = 0.4 in test7, so the viscosity coefficient is uniform. Single precision: rel 1e-5 on grad_mag and the propagation term, 2e-5 on the total tendency (a sum of the two). (EqWeFiC: this repo selects the discretisation per test, so the rules the upstream component imports at model level are imported here, together with the matching per-axis weno5_eno1_D1x/D1y_extrapolate_bc for psi_x/psi_y.)",
       "parameter_overrides": {
         "Lx": 2000.0,
         "Ly": 2000.0,
         "fire_viscosity": 0.4,
         "bdy_eno1_cells": 10,
         "weno_band_cells": 4
       },
       "expression_template_imports": [
        {"ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/weno5_eno1_norm_D2_extrapolate_bc.esm", "bindings": {"NX": 80, "NY": 80}},
        {"ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/weno5_eno1_D1x_extrapolate_bc.esm", "bindings": {"NX": 80, "NY": 80}},
        {"ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/weno5_eno1_D1y_extrapolate_bc.esm", "bindings": {"NX": 80, "NY": 80}},
        {"ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/central_D2x_extrapolate_bc.esm", "bindings": {"NX": 80, "NY": 80}},
        {"ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/central_D2y_extrapolate_bc.esm", "bindings": {"NX": 80, "NY": 80}},
        {"ref": "./tests/weno5_step20_stage1_inputs.esm"}
       ],
       "time_span": {
         "start": 0.0,
         "end": 1.0
       },
       "assertions": [
         {
           "variable": "grad_mag",
           "time": 0.0,
           "coords": {
             "x": 1,
             "y": 1
           },
           "expected": 0.9607469439506531,
           "tolerance": {
             "rel": 1e-05,
             "abs": 1e-06
           }
         },
         {
           "variable": "tend_adv",
           "time": 0.0,
           "coords": {
             "x": 1,
             "y": 1
           },
           "expected": -0.01707698591053486,
           "tolerance": {
             "rel": 1e-05,
             "abs": 1e-07
           }
         },
         {
           "variable": "tend",
           "time": 0.0,
           "coords": {
             "x": 1,
             "y": 1
           },
           "expected": -0.01707698591053486,
           "tolerance": {
             "rel": 2e-05,
             "abs": 1e-06
           }
         },
         {
           "variable": "grad_mag",
           "time": 0.0,
           "coords": {
             "x": 1,
             "y": 80
           },
           "expected": 0.956847608089447,
           "tolerance": {
             "rel": 1e-05,
             "abs": 1e-06
           }
         },
         {
           "variable": "tend_adv",
           "time": 0.0,
           "coords": {
             "x": 1,
             "y": 80
           },
           "expected": -0.4924148619174957,
           "tolerance": {
             "rel": 1e-05,
             "abs": 1e-07
           }
         },
         {
           "variable": "tend",
           "time": 0.0,
           "coords": {
             "x": 1,
             "y": 80
           },
           "expected": -0.4924148619174957,
           "tolerance": {
             "rel": 2e-05,
             "abs": 1e-06
           }
         },
         {
           "variable": "grad_mag",
           "time": 0.0,
           "coords": {
             "x": 80,
             "y": 1
           },
           "expected": 0.949800431728363,
