     {
      "id": "weno5_eno1_step20_stage1",
      "description": "Reference: NCAR fire_behavior test7 (80x80 fire cells of 25 m, dt = 0.5 s, num_tiles = 1) with the shipped namelist, i.e. the DEFAULT scheme fire_upwinding = 9 (hybrid: 5th-order Jiang-Shu WENO5 within fire_lsm_band_ngp = 4 cells of the front, upwind side selected by the wind-relative propagation sign, first-order ENO1 minmod elsewhere and within BDY_ENO1 = 10 cells of the walls, one-cell guarded linear-extrapolation halo), default real32 build, dumped in-model by the ctessum-claude/fire_behavior fork (c9dda02, -DESM_DUMP=ON): ls_tend dump call 58 = Runge-Kutta stage 1 of step 20 (t = 10 s). The inputs psi, ros and the mid-flame wind uf, vf are the full 80x80 dumped fields injected as [x, y] const fields; this test imports EarthSciDiscretizations' weno5_eno1_norm_D2_extrapolate_bc (|grad psi|) and weno5_eno1_D1x/D1y_extrapolate_bc (the per-axis derivatives diff2x, diff2y that also give the normal), with bdy_eno1_cells = 10 and weno_band_cells = 4 (the rules' free names), and central_D2x/D2y_extrapolate_bc for the viscosity term's second differences (fire_behavior's (diffrx - difflx) with the same extrapolated ghost, which makes the wall-cell second difference vanish when the ghost is the linear one). Asserted at 16 cells: 8 cells inside the WENO band around the front (|lfn| < 100 m, 11 <= i, j <= 70; the band spans i 13-28, j 56-69 at this step and the selector signo = (grad4 psi . U) d4 psi changes sign across it, so both upwind orientations are exercised), 3 ENO1 far-field cells, 2 cells inside the 10-cell wall strip (ENO1 by the index rule) and 3 wall cells (i = 1, j = 1, and the corner (80, 80)), where the guarded extrapolation ghost enters; per cell psi_x, psi_y (the dumped diff2x, diff2y), grad_mag (grad), nvx, nvy, tend_adv and tend. fire_viscosity = fire_viscosity_bg = 0.4, so the viscosity coefficient is uniform (viscosity_var = 0.4 on every cell of the dump). Single precision: rel 1e-5 on grad_mag and the propagation term, 2e-5 on the per-axis derivatives, the normal and the total tendency, with absolute floors for values near zero. The whole-field agreement of the transcribed scheme with the dump was checked offline in a NumPy replica: grad <= 7.4e-7 relative, diff2x/y <= 1.3e-5 relative on values above 1e-3, tend <= 1.1e-5, i.e. real32 roundoff.",
      "parameter_overrides": {"Lx": 2000.0, "Ly": 2000.0, "fire_viscosity": 0.4, "bdy_eno1_cells": 10, "weno_band_cells": 4},
      "expression_template_imports": [
       {"ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/weno5_eno1_norm_D2_extrapolate_bc.esm", "bindings": {"NX": 80, "NY": 80}},
       {"ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/weno5_eno1_D1x_extrapolate_bc.esm", "bindings": {"NX": 80, "NY": 80}},
       {"ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/weno5_eno1_D1y_extrapolate_bc.esm", "bindings": {"NX": 80, "NY": 80}},
       {"ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/central_D2x_extrapolate_bc.esm", "bindings": {"NX": 80, "NY": 80}},
       {"ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/central_D2y_extrapolate_bc.esm", "bindings": {"NX": 80, "NY": 80}},
       {"ref": "./tests/weno5_eno1_step20_stage1_inputs.esm"}
