      "description": "fire_upwinding = 7, PURE 5th-order WENO -- the third of the eleven upwinding options to be covered, after 9 (the default hybrid) and 4 (classical Godunov). Option 7 is not a separate discretization: physics/level_set_mod.F90 case (7) is byte-for-byte case (9)'s in-band branch with the `abs(lfn) < threshold_hlu` test removed, so the SAME EarthSciDiscretizations weno5_eno1 rules reproduce it once weno_band_cells is set past the domain diagonal (1e6 cells x 25 m here, against the 2828 m diagonal). The ENO1 strip within bdy_eno1_cells = 10 of the wall is NOT part of the case statement and still applies, which is why the wall cells (5,40), (75,40) and (11,11) are asserted too. Reference: the test7 standalone rerun with fire_upwinding = 7 (data/eqwefic/dumps/fire/run_weno5/esm_dump_ls_tend_58.json, real32, gfortran 13.3 -O2 in the EqWeFiC container), Runge-Kutta stage 1 of step 20. The option is genuinely discriminating: against the fire_upwinding = 9 run of the same case, 3480 of the 6400 interior cells have a different tendency and the largest difference is 1.30 m/s, e.g. -0.02769 against -0.02686 at (40,40) where |lfn| = 646 m, five times the 100 m hybrid band. Near the front, where both schemes are in band, the two runs still agree to the last real32 digit at step 20. rel 2e-5, the same tolerance as the hybrid test, because the WENO5 smoothness weights amplify real32 rounding. Note: the five rule imports bind NX/NY to the literal 80, not to the metaparameter names -- a TEST-level import is injected after the model's index sets are resolved, so binding a symbol there raises template_import_index_set_conflict. The MODEL-level grid import binds the names, which is where the metaparameter has to be honoured.",
