      "id": "weno5_blend_step20_stage1",
      "description": "fire_upwinding = 10, the WENO5/ENO1 scheme with a cosine BLENDING ZONE -- the fourth of the eleven upwinding options covered, after 9 (the default hard-edged hybrid), 4 (classical Godunov) and 7 (pure WENO5). Where option 9 switches abruptly from WENO5 to ENO1 at |psi| = B = weno_band_cells dx = 100 m, option 10 keeps WENO5 out to B, tapers with mask = 0.5 (1 + cos(pi (|psi| - B)/B)) over B < |psi| <= 2B, and is pure ENO1 beyond -- diff2 = mask diff2_weno + (1 - mask) diff2_eno. Lowered by the new EarthSciDiscretizations rule weno5_eno1_blend_norm_D2_extrapolate_bc, whose stencils write that mask as one clamped expression rather than three branches. IT IS GENUINELY DISCRIMINATING, and in exactly the place the physics says it should be: against the fire_upwinding = 9 run of the same case, 185 interior cells have a different tendency and 173 of them lie inside the blending zone, which holds 233 cells; the largest difference is 0.468 m/s and the largest anywhere OUTSIDE the zone is 2.0e-3. The five cells (11,57), (11,58), (11,59), (11,62) and (21,60) are in the zone (|psi| = 139 to 152 m, mask 0.42 to 0.61); (17,57) at |psi| = 54 m is inside B and therefore pure WENO5; (18,64), (20,66), (40,40) and (12,12) are unchanged from the option-9 run to the last real32 digit, which is the check that the blend does not disturb cells it should not touch. Reference: data/eqwefic/dumps/fire/run_blend/esm_dump_ls_tend_58.json, real32, rel 2e-5. The rule reads a free name pi_blend, which this component now takes from the fire constants library (fire_behavior's own truncated PI = 3.1415926, share/constants_mod.F90:18).",
