     {
      "id": "weno3_eno1_step20_stage1",
      "description": "fire_upwinding = 8, the hybrid WENO3/ENO1 scheme -- the fifth of the eleven upwinding options covered, after 9 (the default hard-edged WENO5/ENO1 hybrid), 4 (classical Godunov), 7 (pure WENO5) and 10 (WENO5/ENO1 with a cosine blending zone). physics/level_set_mod.F90 case (8) is case (9) with Select_weno5 replaced by Select_weno3: same band test |psi| < weno_band_cells*dx, same ENO1 wall band, same fourth-order wind-relative upwind selector, a two-stencil third-order Jiang-Shu reconstruction instead of a three-stencil fifth-order one. It needed a NEW EarthSciDiscretizations rule family (weno3_eno1_norm_D2_extrapolate_bc and the two per-axis rules, over the new stencils weno3_js_face_recon, weno3_js_upwind_D1 and weno3_eno1_D1x/D1y_interior): there was no WENO3 at all on cartesian_uniform_2d, and the only WENO3 anywhere in that library is the 1-D weno3_recon, which is WENO-Z (weights gamma_k(1 + (tau3/(eps+beta_k))^2), tau3 = |beta0 - beta1|) rather than the classical gamma_k/(beta_k + eps)^2 this code computes, so it could not be reused. IT IS DISCRIMINATING, and maximally so: applied to this run's own psi field, options 8 and 9 give a different tendency in 175 of the 6400 cells -- which is EVERY cell the WENO branch touches on this state (175 cells are both inside the band and outside the 10-cell ENO1 wall strip) -- and agree to exactly zero difference in all 6225 others. The largest difference is 0.550 m/s in the tendency at (22,62) and 0.377 in |grad psi|. The ten asserted in-band cells are the ten largest of those differences (0.067 to 0.550 m/s); (40,40) and (12,12) are ENO1 cells outside the band and (5,5) is inside the ENO1 wall strip, all three identical under both schemes, which is the check that the third-order reconstruction does not leak outside the band. Swapping weno5_eno1_norm_D2_extrapolate_bc and its two per-axis rules back in, with this run's own psi still bound, fails 27 of these 31 assertions (236/263 for the file) and leaves exactly the four control-cell ones green. Reference: data/eqwefic/dumps/fire/run_weno3/esm_dump_ls_tend_58.json -- NCAR fire_behavior test7 (80x80 fire cells of 25 m, dt = 0.5 s, num_tiles = 1) rerun with fire_upwinding = 8, otherwise the namelist of the option-10 rerun, default real32 build, fork ctessum-claude/fire_behavior c9dda02 with -DESM_DUMP=ON; ls_tend dump call 58 = Runge-Kutta stage 1 of step 20 (t = 10 s). rel 2e-5.",
